    "title": "Mobile Bay Walk to End Alzheimer's taking place in Foley this November - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Summer Poole ,\n1 hours ago\nVideo above: ‘News 5 Now’ — Top Stories from Sept. 16, 2026\nFOLEY, Ala. (WKRG) — The Mobile Bay Walk to End Alzheimer's is taking place this November in Foley.\nClarke County deputies say argument over dog led to fatal attack According to event organizers, the walk will take place at OWA Parks and Recreation on Nov. 14.\nRegistration will begin at 9 a.m., with the opening ceremony starting at 10 a.m.\nThe route is two miles long and will take place rain or shine, unless there is severe weather.\nMobile murder suspect moved to fast-track offender docket Registration is open online . Donations to the Alzheimer's Association can also be made online.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WKRG News 5.",
    "summary": "Video above: ‘News 5 Now’ — Top Stories from Sept. 16, 2026 FOLEY, Ala. (WKRG) — The Mobile Bay Walk to End Alzheimer's is taking place this November in Foley. Clarke County deputies say argument over dog led to fatal attack According to event organizers, the walk will take place at OWA Parks and Recreation on Nov. 14. Registration will begin at 9 a.m., with the opening ceremony starting at 10 a.m. The route is two miles long and will take place rain or shine, unless there is severe weather.",
